### Example: Domain — `IFoo.cs` + `Foo.cs`

Every domain type has an interface AND a POCO at `Domain/` root.  
Canonical: `find_symbol("IWeatherForecast")`, `find_symbol("WeatherForecast")`

```csharp
// Domain/IWeatherForecast.cs
public interface IWeatherForecast
{
    DateTime StartDate { get; set; }
    DateTime EndDate { get; set; }
    int TemperatureC { get; set; }
    int TemperatureF => 32 + (int)(TemperatureC / 0.5556);
    string? Summary { get; set; }
}

// Domain/WeatherForecast.cs
public class WeatherForecast : IWeatherForecast
{
    public DateTime EndDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime StartDate { get; set; }
    public int TemperatureC { get; set; }
    public int TemperatureF => 32 + (int)(TemperatureC / 0.5556);
    public string? Summary { get; set; }
}
```

---

### Example: CQRS — query record + handler

All CQRS marker interfaces come from `Xpo.Common.Cqrs`. One file per handler: result type + query/command record + optional feature interface + handler implementation.  
Canonical: `find_symbol("GetWeatherQueryHandler")`

```csharp
using Xpo.Common.Cqrs;

// TResult — response shape returned to the caller.
public class GetWeatherQueryResult : IWeatherForecast
{
    public DateTime StartDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EndDate { get; set; }
    public int TemperatureC { get; set; }
    public string? Summary { get; set; }
}

// TRequest — implements IAsyncQuery<TResult>. Add validation-attributed fields here as inputs grow.
public class GetWeatherQuery : IAsyncQuery<List<GetWeatherQueryResult>> { }

// Optional feature-scoped interface — useful for mocking in tests without touching the generic type.
public interface IGetWeatherQueryHandler
{
    Task<List<GetWeatherQueryResult>> Handle(GetWeatherQuery query);
}

// Handler — implements both the feature interface and the Xpo.Common.Cqrs generic.
// Discovered and dispatched by IApiService; never resolved directly by endpoints.
public class GetWeatherQueryHandler : IGetWeatherQueryHandler,
    IAsyncQueryHandler<GetWeatherQuery, List<GetWeatherQueryResult>>
{
    private readonly IWeatherService _weatherService;

    public GetWeatherQueryHandler(IWeatherService weatherService)
    {
        _weatherService = weatherService;
    }

    public async Task<List<GetWeatherQueryResult>> Handle(GetWeatherQuery query)
    {
        var weather = await _weatherService.GetWeatherAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);

        return weather.Select(w => new GetWeatherQueryResult
        {
            StartDate    = w.StartDate,
            EndDate      = w.EndDate,
            TemperatureC = w.TemperatureC,
            Summary      = w.Summary,
        }).ToList();
    }
}
```

Command example — implements the domain interface so the endpoint can bind the request body directly:  
Canonical: `find_symbol("SaveWeatherForecastCommand")`

```csharp
using Xpo.Common.Cqrs;

// TRequest — implements IAsyncCommand + the domain interface (no separate DTO needed).
public class SaveWeatherForecastCommand : IAsyncCommand, IWeatherForecast
{
    [Required] public DateTime StartDate { get; set; }
    [Required] public DateTime EndDate   { get; set; }
    [Range(-100, 100, ErrorMessage = "TemperatureC must be a plausible Celsius value.")]
    public int TemperatureC { get; set; }
    [StringLength(120)] public string? Summary { get; set; }
}

// Optional feature-scoped interface for test isolation.
public interface ISaveWeatherForecastCommandHandler
{
    Task Handle(SaveWeatherForecastCommand command);
}

// Handler — implements both the feature interface and IAsyncCommandHandler<T>.
public class SaveWeatherForecastCommandHandler
    : ISaveWeatherForecastCommandHandler,
      IAsyncCommandHandler<SaveWeatherForecastCommand>
{
    private readonly IWeatherService _weatherService;

    public SaveWeatherForecastCommandHandler(IWeatherService weatherService)
    {
        _weatherService = weatherService;
    }

    public async Task Handle(SaveWeatherForecastCommand command)
    {
        await _weatherService.SaveWeatherAsync(command).ConfigureAwait(false);
    }
}
```

