### Example: API unit test — xUnit + Moq

Before writing any test: `find_symbol("SaveWeatherForecastCommandHandlerTests")` as canonical.  
Layout: mirror source tree exactly — `Foo.cs` → `FooTests.cs`, same relative path.

```csharp
public class SaveWeatherForecastCommandHandlerTests
{
    private readonly Mock<IWeatherService> _weatherService;

    public SaveWeatherForecastCommandHandlerTests()
    {
        _weatherService = new Mock<IWeatherService>();
    }

    private SaveWeatherForecastCommandHandler GetHandler()
        => new SaveWeatherForecastCommandHandler(_weatherService.Object);

    [Fact]
    public async Task Handle_DispatchesForecastToService()
    {
        // arrange
        var command = new SaveWeatherForecastCommand
        {
            StartDate    = new DateTime(2026, 5, 14, 9, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc),
            EndDate      = new DateTime(2026, 5, 14, 10, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc),
            TemperatureC = 18,
            Summary      = "Partly Cloudy",
        };
        _weatherService
            .Setup(s => s.SaveWeatherAsync(It.IsAny<IWeatherForecast>()))
            .Returns(Task.CompletedTask);
        var handler = GetHandler();

        // act
        await handler.Handle(command);

        // assert
        _weatherService.Verify(s => s.SaveWeatherAsync(It.Is<IWeatherForecast>(f =>
            f.StartDate    == command.StartDate    &&
            f.EndDate      == command.EndDate      &&
            f.TemperatureC == command.TemperatureC &&
            f.Summary      == command.Summary)), Times.Once);
    }
}
```

**Rules:**
- Mock fields named after the dependency (`_weatherService`, not `_mock`). Keep `Mock<>` visible.
- Constructor initialises all mocks with `new Mock<T>()`.
- `GetHandler()` / `GetService()` factory — never `new` the SUT inline in a test.
- `// arrange` / `// act` / `// assert` lower-case comments — all three, in order.
- Async: `public async Task`, never `async void`.
- One assertion focus per test; split when a second assertion describes a separate behaviour.
- Test names describe behaviour: `Handle_DispatchesForecastToService`, not `Test1`. Use the actual method name (`Handle`) as the verb prefix.

**Coverage — business logic only, skip plumbing:**
- ✅ Handler dispatches the right shape; service maps domain → entity; branching on validation failure.
- ❌ Pass-through getters, `ArgumentNullException` guards, DI registration, attribute routing.

