## Creating a new cache provider

Inherit `CacheProviderBase`. Only `QualifyKey` is mandatory.

Key convention: `{domain}:{feature}:{key}` — keeps entries isolated across features in a shared Redis instance.

```csharp
// Services/Caching/OrderCacheProvider.cs
using Rxo.Common.Redis;
using Rxo.Platform.Api.Sandbox.Services.Caching;
using Xpo.Auth.Data.Caching;

namespace Rxo.Platform.Api.Sandbox.Services.Caching
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Redis cache provider for the order feature namespace.
    /// All keys are prefixed with <c>sandbox:orders:</c>.
    /// Group key <c>sandbox:orders:group</c> flushes the entire namespace.
    /// </summary>
    public class OrderCacheProvider : CacheProviderBase
    {
        public OrderCacheProvider(IRxoRedisCache cache) : base(cache) { }

        protected override string QualifyKey(string key) => $"sandbox:orders:{key}";

        public override string GroupKey() => QualifyKey("group");
    }
}
```

To change the TTL, override `CacheExpiration`:

```csharp
protected override TimeSpan CacheExpiration { get; set; } = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(15);
```

