## Registration — nothing to do

`ServiceModule` auto-discovers all `ICacheProvider` implementations via assembly scanning:

```csharp
// ServiceModule.cs
builder.RegisterAssemblyTypes(Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly())
    .As(typeof(ICacheProvider))
    .AsImplementedInterfaces()
    .SingleInstance();
```

Adding `OrderCacheProvider` to the assembly is sufficient — it is registered automatically as `ICacheProvider` and as its own concrete type.

Inject it in a handler or service by its concrete type or via `ICacheProvider`:

```csharp
public class GetOrderQueryHandler : IGetOrderQueryHandler, IAsyncQueryHandler<GetOrderQuery, GetOrderQueryResult>
{
    private readonly IOrderService _orderService;
    private readonly OrderCacheProvider _cache;   // concrete type — unambiguous

    public GetOrderQueryHandler(IOrderService orderService, OrderCacheProvider cache)
    {
        _orderService = orderService;
        _cache = cache;
    }

    public async Task<GetOrderQueryResult> HandleAsync(GetOrderQuery query)
    {
        var cached = await _cache.GetAsync<GetOrderQueryResult>(query.OrderId);
        if (cached != null) return cached;

        var result = await _orderService.GetOrderAsync(query.OrderId);
        await _cache.SetAsync(query.OrderId, result);
        return result;
    }
}
```

